    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7ujkqLl6KRwg"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Model Prep: Create our features matrix (`X`) and target vector (`y`)\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "What should our features be?\n",
        "\n",
        "The `apps` column is our label: the number of applications received by that university.\n",
        "\n",
        "In the cell below, create your `X` and `y` variables."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 90,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "vdrd6mgXKRwg"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X = df.drop(columns=['university', 'accept', 'enroll', 'apps'])\n",
        "y = df['apps']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ztpO2H3CKRwg"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Model Prep: Train/test split\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "We always want to have a holdout set to test our model. Use the `train_test_split` function to split our `X` and `y` variables into a training set and a holdout set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 91,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ysbZSo8-KRwg"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y, random_state=42)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "C_cSgqyzKRwg"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Model Prep: Scaling\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "In the cell below, fit a `StandardScaler` to `X_train` and use it to transform both `X_train` and `X_test`. This is especially important when we learn about `Ridge` and `Lasso` next week!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 92,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SCqvEJqEKRwg"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "ss = StandardScaler()\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train = ss.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
        "X_test = ss.transform(X_test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cAUo7qc6KRwh"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Model Prep: Instantiate our model\n",
        "---\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 93,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MossaThIKRwh"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "lr = LinearRegression()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "URy94gN4KRwh"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Evaluation\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `.score` to evaluate the model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 94,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mnS9dmP_KRwh",
        "outputId": "4f4dd586-dae9-4434-bbfe-0c026333619e",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Training R2 = 0.8269793960769836\n",
            "Testing R2 = 0.7915343092045559\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "lr.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Training R2 = {lr.score(X_train, y_train)}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Testing R2 = {lr.score(X_test, y_test)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Vu_g1sjkKRwh"
      },
      "source": [
        "# LINE Assumptions\n",
        "---\n"
